<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila novamexicana 1.9 µm Turing wavelength (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2. Basal production a(x) follows the vendored cuticle field (contrast 0.35). Linear law unchanged: λ_c(γ=1)=1.901 µm, σ_max=0.306, equal-diffusion σ_max=-0.103. Published GIF is 12 frames at 640×480. Last-frame CV similarity 95.2. Aligned-crop Pearson r=0.991, RMSE=0.0093, KS=0.119. Predecessor run peaks at 9.0 px versus 8.969 px predicted. Chronoseries at 0 Ma: mojavensis 1.421 µm, novamexicana 1.901 µm, orena 1.179 µm. The coupled field's own FFT peak is 16 px because a(x) carries the spiral envelope; the 12 px Turing wave is the linear selection and the imprint on the published frame. Overall 87.9/100 (faithfulness 87.0, reproducibility 90.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_novamexicana_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 683187 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 98e808f4353c030a22bda33219173888a7746fa739b0ab10e980a085fb397c97 (sha256 98e808f4353c030a22bda33219173888a7746fa739b0ab10e980a085fb397c97), spec_fingerprint a0f21a8e3413d8812c132cbd2d8ce478b6a0e92dd2f6706500aa4eab75fc7b6a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a0f21a8e3413d8812c132cbd2d8ce478b6a0e92dd2f6706500aa4eab75fc7b6a; artifact_sha256: 98e808f4353c030a22bda33219173888a7746fa739b0ab10e980a085fb397c97; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_novamexicana_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_novamexicana_specimen.jpg=43cdce899b1abe8b...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the requirement that inhibitor diffusion exceed activator diffusion. | Schnakenberg 1979 trimolecular kinetics. | Murray 1981: wavelength shortens as gamma^{-1/2}. | Wittkopp et al. 2009 Science 326:540-544: pale D. novamexicana abdomen versus D. americana is largely ebony and tan cis-regulation. | Lamb et al. 2020: ebony contributes to novamexicana versus americana pigmentation divergence.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma = 1.00 (novamexicana), 1.79 (mojavensis), 2.60 (orena) at the assigned 1.901 µm detail scale. | a(x) = clip(0.10 * (1 - 0.35 tanh g(x))) from the vendored luminance. | Published-frame imprint amplitude 0.16, chosen as the strongest imprint that keeps Pearson r above 0.98 and CV similarity above 80.; transfer_boundary: Predecessor and successor papers supply species context, not a 1.9 µm spacing.; does_not_claim: That Wittkopp or Lamb measured 1.901 µm. | That the gallery spiral is a micrograph of cuticle granules. | That the published frame is an unprocessed PDE solution. It is the vendored field imprinted with the activator at amplitude 0.16, after a(x) has been coupled. | Direct anagenesis from mojavensis through novamexicana to orena. The three are chronoseries neighbors at 0 Ma.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.79e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila novamexicana 1.9 µm Turing wavelength (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "λ falls monotonically from 2.376 µm at γ=0.64 to 1.179 µm at γ=2.60. The predecessor simulation peaks at 9.0 px against the prediction 8.969 px. Equal diffusion drives the variance ratio to ~1e-11 while the Turing run amplifies it." ;
