<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila novamexicana 1.9 µm Turing wavelength (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Drosophila novamexicana)",
        "Drosophila novamexicana 1.9 µm Turing wavelength (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila novamexicana morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila novamexicana specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila novamexicana" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Direct anagenesis from mojavensis through novamexicana to orena. The three are chronoseries neighbors at 0 Ma.",
        "does_not_claim: That Wittkopp or Lamb measured 1.901 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That the gallery spiral is a micrograph of cuticle granules.",
        "does_not_claim: That the published frame is an unprocessed PDE solution. It is the vendored field imprinted with the activator at amplitude 0.16, after a(x) has been coupled.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Published-frame imprint amplitude 0.16, chosen as the strongest imprint that keeps Pearson r above 0.98 and CV similarity above 80.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: a(x) = clip(0.10 * (1 - 0.35 tanh g(x))) from the vendored luminance.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: gamma = 1.00 (novamexicana), 1.79 (mojavensis), 2.60 (orena) at the assigned 1.901 µm detail scale.",
        "reported_in_source: Lamb et al. 2020: ebony contributes to novamexicana versus americana pigmentation divergence.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981: wavelength shortens as gamma^{-1/2}.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 trimolecular kinetics.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the requirement that inhibitor diffusion exceed activator diffusion.",
        "reported_in_source: Wittkopp et al. 2009 Science 326:540-544: pale D. novamexicana abdomen versus D. americana is largely ebony and tan cis-regulation.",
        "transfer_boundary: Predecessor and successor papers supply species context, not a 1.9 µm spacing." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila novamexicana (Southwestern Desert Riparian Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-novamexicana-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_novamexicana_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila novamexicana; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the requirement that inhibitor diffusion exceed activator diffusion. | Schnakenberg 1979 trimolecular kinetics. | Murray 1981: wavelength shortens as gamma^{-1/2}. | Wittkopp et al. 2009 Science 326:540-544: pale D. novamexicana abdomen versus D. americana is largely ebony and tan cis-regulation. | Lamb et al. 2020: ebony contributes to novamexicana versus americana pigmentation divergence.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma = 1.00 (novamexicana), 1.79 (mojavensis), 2.60 (orena) at the assigned 1.901 µm detail scale. | a(x) = clip(0.10 * (1 - 0.35 tanh g(x))) from the vendored luminance. | Published-frame imprint amplitude 0.16, chosen as the strongest imprint that keeps Pearson r above 0.98 and CV similarity above 80.; transfer_boundary: Predecessor and successor papers supply species context, not a 1.9 µm spacing.; does_not_claim: That Wittkopp or Lamb measured 1.901 µm. | That the gallery spiral is a micrograph of cuticle granules. | That the published frame is an unprocessed PDE solution. It is the vendored field imprinted with the activator at amplitude 0.16, after a(x) has been coupled. | Direct anagenesis from mojavensis through novamexicana to orena. The three are chronoseries neighbors at 0 Ma.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
